# Memory — Cross-Project Index

> Template for `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/MEMORY.md`. Auto-loaded into every session's context.
> Replace placeholders, delete sections you don't use. Goal: a one-line pointer per topic, no narrative.
> Soft cap: ≤200 lines so the entire file fits in context. Lines past 200 may be truncated.

Format: one-line pointers. Detail lives in project CLAUDE.md, plan files, or `memory/learnings/`.

---

## Current State (YYYY-MM-DD / S{N} / brief headline)

- **Phase**: <which phase / spec / refactor is active; ≤2 lines>
- **Next**: <the single next concrete action; quote the artifact you're acting on, don't paraphrase>

- **Session {N} (YYYY-MM-DD)**: <one-line summary>. → `memory/learnings/YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md`
- **Session {N-1} (YYYY-MM-DD)**: <one-line summary>. → `memory/learnings/YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md`
- **Session {N-2} (YYYY-MM-DD)**: <one-line summary>. → `memory/learnings/YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md`

---

## Active Projects

### Project A (added YYYY-MM-DD)
- **Dir**: `path/to/repo` · **Plan**: `path/to/plan.md` · **Learnings**: `path/to/learnings/` ({N} files)
- <2-4 lines of structural context — decisions, scope, constraints — NOT activity log>
- **Next**: <single concrete action OR an open question gating progress>

### Project B (added YYYY-MM-DD)
- **Dir**: `path/to/repo` · **Detail**: `memory/project_<slug>.md`
- <2-4 lines>
- **Open before any work**: <preconditions / blockers>

